WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.480
Snake, Rattle and Roll, brilliant 3D graphics and a colorful new duo, Rattle and Roll.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.800
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:32.860
I'm Mike.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.180
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.500
And honestly, if you didn't read the back of the box, or you just didn't read the manual,

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:47.440
or you didn't read anything online, you wouldn't assume automatically that the snakes names were

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.020
Rattle and Roll.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.320
I certainly didn't.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.220
I just thought it was a cute play on words.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.340
But are they like, is snake their last name?

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.600
Is it like Rattlesnake and Roll Snake?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.640
Are they brothers? Oh no, they're just snakes, Mike.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.620
So, oh, so snakes only get first names, right?

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.980
Right. Yeah, actually that's true, right?

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:14.840
Like, my dog, whose name is Phoebe, I do call her at the vet Phoebe Esposito.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:20.160
So I guess Rattle does, is owed some kind, like he would be Rattle Esposito though, right?

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:21.940
Well, maybe for you.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.920
Maybe for you. Because that's my last name.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:25.980
So he would be my pet.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.780
But what about if I played the game?

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.160
If you played the game.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.640
Oh, I see. So during the game, because.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.460
So it would still be Rattle Esposito?

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:39.120
Yeah, you know, and it's true, because this is a rare game, so just bring in some rare logic.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:46.240
Like Banjo and Kazooie don't have last names, but Donkey and Diddy do.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.720
They're both Kong.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.400
Hmm. But that's like more Nintendo rules than anything.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.220
I'm sure they would have liked to have just called him Diddy instead of Diddy Kong.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:02:02.020
It's gotta be like the Mario, the first Mario movie where like one of their first names is also both of their last names.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.140
That's like Rattle, Rattle, and Roll Rattle.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.440
Yeah. So Mario was the last name?

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.620
Yeah, Mario, Mario, and Luigi Mario.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.540
Hmm. They thought that was so funny in the movie.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.440
Like they thought like, oh, we've really got something clever here.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.740
That's why they're called the Super Mario Brothers.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.840
Are we talking about? Because their last name is Mario.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.540
The live action? Are we talking about?

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.760
The live action. Yeah.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.900
Oh, okay. The only one worth talking about.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.700
Yeah. The other one is like, you know, sure, it was big at the box office, but it's not worth talking about.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:38.540
Now, what if they made a modern Pixar style Rattle, Snake, Roll game?

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.740
It would be called Snake, Rattle, and Roll for sure for just brand recognition.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:50.740
But yeah, what we would have is hopefully a great isometric Pixar movie.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:55.100
Because that's what we were promised here in this video game.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:03:02.380
We are playing as, I'll just say it, you're probably only playing as Rattle unless you're playing with two players, in which case you unlock Roll.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:10.360
And you are in these isometric 3D worlds where you are starting off just as, you're not a full snake.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:11.980
You're just the snake head.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:18.760
And I think that leans a little bit into the game Snake, right?

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.140
That we all played on our Nokia phones before cell phones.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.620
I would say that that would be the thing you think about.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.220
Right? So you're like a little snake head.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.420
You don't really think about the horror of just being a snake head.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.660
Right, right. They don't look horrified.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:42.700
You eat some of those nibbly pibblies and you grow into a larger snake.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:49.000
A snake that the size demands you to be to complete a particular level.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.560
You can't just be a snake with just a head.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:53.640
That's not acceptable.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.560
The course will not let you out.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:04:00.040
The only way to get out is to ring a weigh-in bell.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:04.940
So is it because you need to be long enough to hit the top of the bell?

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:08.920
Or you need to be long enough which makes you heavy enough to weigh in?

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.060
Yeah, I think it's about your weight.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:18.020
Yeah. I like the idea that it's just being long enough to touch the top and kind of like ring it yourself.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.300
Yeah, but he doesn't do that.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.440
He doesn't. He just sits on the scale.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.580
He doesn't do that, but that's what it's making up.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.900
You think about it. The whole thing is that you're getting longer.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.900
So now I'm just getting fatter?

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.740
It's longer? I mean... No, you're getting longer.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.460
It makes sense. It still adds weight to you.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.620
Yeah, there's still mass.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:42.180
Okay. I mean, you go on a scale at the end and one of those little things on a carnival when you hit the hammer, I guess,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.060
thing goes up and rings the bell, right?

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:49.040
Yeah. Yeah, but I think it would be more fun if he rang the bell.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:50.940
Okay. I have notes.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.040
I have notes for the developer.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:53.840
That's good to know.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.060
We'll keep that in mind.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.400
Here's another note.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:02.040
When you're starting the game and it has one player or two players on the options menu,

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:11.040
it's not entirely clear that that little sparkly thing to the left of that is your selection.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:14.860
It's a different kind of graphic than I'm used to.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.660
Oh, I don't...

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:18.420
It looks like it's just part of the background.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:19.960
I know what you're talking about.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:20.980
On the menu screen?

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:23.700
Yeah, on the menu screen, that is like...

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.580
It's sparkling, right?

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:29.760
But technically, all of one player should just be sparkling.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.860
So this way you know that that's the option you're highlighted on,

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:36.020
but instead it's just to the left of it in the black void.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:41.380
So it's not entirely clear that that's me, the cursor, choosing one player.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:45.020
It's fine because it starts you on that and you're just going to hit A anyway.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.140
But when it moved, I was startled.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.880
Do you see yourself as the cursor?

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.420
Do you have a first-person feeling as a cursor?

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.520
As a cursor, I feel like I...

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:04.260
Yeah, when I'm holding a mouse and a keyboard at the same time,

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.940
and I'm moving the mouse...

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.120
You get motion sick. Yeah.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.940
I'm moving the mouse on the computer.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:14.140
I do follow that mouse around as if it's my body, as if it's my hand.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.460
Okay. That's cute.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:16.900
Okay, back to the game.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.200
So let's talk about the controls,

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.360
because that's probably going to be the thing that's going to be

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.000
the most interesting thing to talk about here.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.240
You, as I mentioned, it's an isometric game.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:30.560
So we've played some pretty recent examples of this

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:33.800
where we've been like sometimes hot,

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:39.860
but for the most times not too hot on the free 3D controls on the NES.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:45.000
How does, especially Snake Round and Roll, as a platforming game,

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.200
how does it handle?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:53.100
So, like any isometric game with a D-pad,

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:57.560
they have a very important question to answer,

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.800
very important decision to make,

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:04.360
and that's what's going to happen when you press down.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:11.080
And then there's also, like, what's going to happen when you press left.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.700
Like, they have to skew it in one direction or another,

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.580
and I don't think there's, like, a true correct answer here

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:23.560
as to whether down means down right or down left,

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.760
because that's what isometric does,

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:31.840
or if it's just completely, like, down means down on the screen,

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.200
and you kind of have to always be pressing diagonals

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:39.560
if you want to go in the isometric north, east, west, south.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:42.920
And they chose.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:46.700
I think down makes you go down and to the right on the screen.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:47.920
Correct me if I'm wrong.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:52.880
And that can be kind of confusing for a while,

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.660
but then after some time you kind of get used to it,

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.880
especially because I think that the platforming in this game,

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:06.060
it's kind of squishy enough, it's a little forgiving,

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:11.420
but it's definitely the brain buster for a little while.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:15.580
Yeah, I'm that way with any isometric game like this.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:18.020
It takes me a while to get used to it,

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:23.500
but I do always end up tilting the controller in the way,

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:28.000
and it works for me in a way so that, you know,

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:32.480
up will be pointing upright or whatever direction up means in this game.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:37.360
And that does make it a lot easier for me over time.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:42.860
But, yeah, it's like this unfortunate limitation to this kind of game on the NES,

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.200
because if there was a joystick or something, it would be no problem.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.240
But obviously there is not.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:53.160
So that is like definitely the first thing anyone notices about this game,

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:54.100
I would think.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:58.960
And the snakes are a bit floaty in their movement and their jumps.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:05.060
And this is a, you know, it's a vertical platformer

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.300
in the sense that you will continue to, you know,

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:12.540
kind of climb up things with the repercussions of falling down and such.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:16.960
Does it become a thing where, you know,

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:21.140
maybe the floatiness is a skill thing?

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:26.080
Or does it become like a frustration point where the floatiness at times,

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:28.120
especially on more precise platforming,

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:32.200
just winds up being something that can easily be a trap for the player?

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:35.780
Yeah, I don't think that the floatiness of the controls

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.840
is really where any frustration is born out of.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:44.800
I think it's a combination of that shift

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:52.740
from like a straight on D-pad to kind of having to go diagonal.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:58.980
And with the perspective itself, like, and how that visually looks.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:07.820
Because isometric, you really, you're kind of removing some important parts

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:10.940
of how you're perceiving three dimensions.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.480
If they've shown, like, they'll have,

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:21.420
they'll have like sections of the screen that maybe they aren't as clearly defined

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:27.760
as like one square and then a wall and then squares above that.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:31.040
It'll be sort of like a little,

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:35.160
it'll be a little like squishy looking on the screen.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:39.000
And you can't really tell what side is higher than the other.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.780
And then you end up trying to make a jump

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.160
and you can't tell if you're just missing the jump

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.240
or if that's actually an impossible jump.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:50.260
I don't know if you guys are picking up what I'm putting down here.

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:51.700
Yeah, I know exactly what you mean.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:56.480
But I did appreciate that they added a very clear, crisp shadow,

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:00.860
which does at least help to alleviate some of that issue.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.300
I mean, it's something that they did even 3D,

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.600
like I know Crash Bandicoot,

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:05.920
which is a full 3D game,

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.920
but like people weren't used to that.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.200
And it is a little weird

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.320
when you're trying to precisely land on something,

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.500
having like that crisp circle below you.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:15.820
And that did help me.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:17.840
Granted, it never really helped me

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:20.660
like the first time I tried to jump onto something

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.020
and then I fall to my death,

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.940
but I would see my shadow afterwards

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:26.540
and it would tell me, oh, I could land on that or I couldn't

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.360
if like, or that's not what I was looking at,

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:29.820
but at least it was some indication.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:32.300
Yeah, I just always had some trouble

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:33.960
gauging height.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:35.900
Yeah, especially thinking like,

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.460
oh, there's certain jumps maybe,

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.040
you know, that you can't make

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.840
next to other jumps that you can.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.320
And I will say that, you know,

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.200
kudos to Rare here,

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:47.600
they did create early on environments

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.820
that kind of welcome you

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:54.500
to master being rattle or roll

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.640
and jumping around without consequence.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.460
Like, yeah, you might hit an enemy

00:11:58.460 --> 00:11:59.980
and lose, you know,

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.280
part of your tail or something.

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:02.420
That's another interesting thing

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:03.480
that like, you know,

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:04.640
you, that's what you,

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.100
you almost like Sonic the Hedgehog

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:07.500
in that way. You lose all your coins.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.080
Like you just lose a piece of your tail.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.540
You don't have like a health bar per se.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.660
So you have,

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:14.620
you have a lot of like,

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:16.760
it's not a sandbox necessarily,

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.480
but the early, earlier levels do allow you

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:21.820
to just kind of get your bearings

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:22.960
and figure all this out

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:24.600
before it just becomes like,

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:30.720
you know, more strict challenge of platforming.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:34.160
Like, I feel like if it went into like pitfalls

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:36.460
and spike deaths

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:38.180
and, you know,

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:40.440
wading tides and stuff early on,

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.700
it would be like a,

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:43.820
too tough a game.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.880
But because I was able to spend some time

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:48.300
just getting my bearings

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.820
with the, the jump itself,

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:52.460
because the whole game basically

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:54.980
is you're a floating snakehead

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:57.120
jumping around and trying to reach,

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:59.720
again, it's vertical. So you're trying to like reach

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:02.340
the next part of these mountainous stages.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:04.780
I do think,

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.900
ultimately, the level designs communicate

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.440
pretty clearly

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:11.960
where you have to go next,

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:12.940
what you have to do.

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:16.020
It's mostly an inviting experience.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.340
It's not necessarily hardcore by any means.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.360
The hardcore part probably comes in

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:22.680
to the challenge of

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.300
the platforming itself

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:25.440
and being able to

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.560
navigate these terrains

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:28.380
once they start

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:29.880
filling them with enemies

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:30.920
and pits

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:32.200
and death traps,

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:33.220
you know? Yeah,

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:35.340
I think the inviting nature of it

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:37.580
is just in how goofy

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:39.480
the, like,

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:41.040
the character design is

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.700
and, you know,

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:44.600
it's got like a nice

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:45.980
soothing color palette

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:47.400
and it just does look nice.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:49.660
But I, I think like there,

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.140
there is still,

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:53.360
like, there's a lot of,

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.840
like, spiky stuff,

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.560
but like, they're not, they're not like hardcore spiky.

00:13:57.760 --> 00:13:59.300
So yeah, I get what you're saying.

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:00.740
Yeah, they're not in the,

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:02.340
they're not in the stage yet.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.060
Like, they're like off to the side.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:07.180
They're kind of like introducing these elements to you.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.380
But, you know,

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:09.760
the game will get hard,

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:10.620
but I think it like,

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:12.440
it progresses nicely.

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.160
Yeah, there's feet.

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:15.920
And you mentioned, you know,

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.400
the fun design of it all.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:18.700
I do think even the enemies

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:19.580
